+## 2026-10-25 signed-direction repair
+
+The imported generator always placed the blue marker at the top-left and drew only nonnegative translation vectors. Consequently an `abs(red-blue)`/down-right shortcut fit the synthetic distribution even though a canonical negative-direction example rejects it.
+
+Version `2.1.0` retains the same rule and construction, then independently reflects the completed input horizontally and vertically with the existing deterministic layout RNG. This preserves the exact relative marker-vector semantics and all motif-copy guarantees while producing both row and column signs and every relative marker corner. No canonical Racket authority changed.
+
+Regression tests first failed on the imported source because no negative vector signs or adversarial witness existed. After the repair, the full task-local suite passed. `workspace/direction_probe.py` is a reusable source-bound probe; it found a generated vector `(1,-2)` whose intended signed-vector output matches protected Racket and differs from the absolute-delta rival. The bounded test does not prove uniqueness against every possible shortcut.
